==Crimean Gothic==

===Etymology===
Probably from an {{etyl|ira|gme-cgo}} language. Compare Avestan {{term|𐬯𐬀𐬙𐬀|tr=sata|lang=ae}}, Sanskrit {{term|शत|tr=śatá|lang=sa}}.

===Numeral===
{{head|gme-cgo|numeral}}

# [[hundred]]
#* 1562, Ogier Ghiselin de Busbecq:
#*: Viginti dicebat stega, triginta treithyen, quadraginta furdeithien, centum '''sada''', hazer mille.

